/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Acts chapters 11-15
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("acts", [
{n:11, name:"Gentiles Receive the Spirit", seal:{ref:"Acts 11:18",verse:"When they heard these things, they held their peace, and glorified God, saying, Then hath God also to the Gentiles granted repentance unto life."}, facts:["Did you know the name 'Christian' was first coined in Antioch, given by watching outsiders to this brand-new fellowship where Jews and Gentiles worshiped side by side (Acts 11:26)?","Did you know Peter did not go to Cornelius alone? Six Jewish believers went with him as witnesses, so no one in Jerusalem could doubt what the Spirit had done (Acts 11:12).","Did you know the prophet Agabus foretold a worldwide famine that came true under Claudius Caesar, and the Antioch church answered with a relief offering for their Judean brothers instead of panic (Acts 11:28-30)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who heard that the Gentiles had also received the word of God?", options:["The apostles and brethren that were in Judaea","The priests serving in the temple","The Roman garrison at Caesarea","The elders of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:1",verse:"And the apostles and brethren that were in Judaea heard that the Gentiles had also received the word of God.", insight:"The news spread fast because it was unheard of: the word of God landing among outsiders."},
{q:"What charge did the circumcision party bring against Peter?", options:["Thou wentest in to men uncircumcised, and didst eat with them","Thou hast denied the law of Moses","Thou hast preached for money","Thou hast baptized without authority"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:3",verse:"Saying, Thou wentest in to men uncircumcised, and didst eat with them.", insight:"Table fellowship was the flashpoint; who you eat with says who you call family."},
{q:"How did Peter answer his critics?", options:["He rehearsed the matter from the beginning, and expounded it by order","He refused to explain himself","He quoted the law back at them","He left Jerusalem at once"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:4",verse:"But Peter rehearsed the matter from the beginning, and expounded it by order unto them, saying,", insight:"Peter told the story in order; a clear testimony disarms suspicion better than a sharp reply."},
{q:"Where was Peter when he saw the vision?", options:["In the city of Joppa, praying","In the temple at Jerusalem","On a ship bound for Caesarea","In the house of Cornelius"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:5",verse:"I was in the city of Joppa praying: and in a trance I saw a vision, A certain vessel descend, as it had been a great sheet, let down from heaven by four corners; and it came even to me:", insight:"God caught Peter in prayer; visions find people who are already talking to heaven."},
{q:"What did Peter see descending from heaven?", options:["A great sheet, let down by four corners","A ladder with angels ascending","A scroll sealed with wax","A pillar of cloud and fire"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:5",verse:"I was in the city of Joppa praying: and in a trance I saw a vision, A certain vessel descend, as it had been a great sheet, let down from heaven by four corners; and it came even to me:", insight:"The sheet held what Peter's traditions forbade; God was lowering his walls as well as his lunch."},
{q:"What kinds of creatures filled the sheet?", options:["Fourfooted beasts, wild beasts, creeping things, and fowls of the air","Only clean lambs and doves","Fish of every kind","Serpents and scorpions alone"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:6",verse:"Upon the which when I had fastened mine eyes, I considered, and saw fourfooted beasts of the earth, and wild beasts, and creeping things, and fowls of the air.", insight:"Every category of unclean creature, gathered in one sheet; God was redrawing the whole map of clean and unclean."},
{q:"What did the voice command Peter?", options:["Arise, Peter; slay and eat","Go, Peter, and preach to the Gentiles","Rise, Peter, and build an altar","Come, Peter, and follow me"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:7",verse:"And I heard a voice saying unto me, Arise, Peter; slay and eat.", insight:"The command struck at Peter's deepest habit; obedience often begins where comfort ends."},
{q:"How did Peter first respond to the voice?", options:["Not so, Lord: for nothing common or unclean hath at any time entered into my mouth","Yes, Lord, at once","Lord, give me time to think","Lord, send another in my place"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:8",verse:"But I said, Not so, Lord: for nothing common or unclean hath at any time entered into my mouth.", insight:"'Not so, Lord' is a contradiction in terms; Peter learned you cannot call Him Lord and refuse Him."},
{q:"What did the voice from heaven answer Peter?", options:["What God hath cleansed, that call not thou common","Do as thou wilt, Peter","The law is abolished forever","Eat only what is clean"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:9",verse:"But the voice answered me again from heaven, What God hath cleansed, that call not thou common.", insight:"God's cleansing outruns our categories; what He has made clean, we dare not call common."},
{q:"How many brethren accompanied Peter to the man's house?", options:["Six","Two","Twelve","Seventy"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:12",verse:"And the spirit bade me go with them, nothing doubting. Moreover these six brethren accompanied me, and we entered into the man’s house:", insight:"Six witnesses walked with Peter; truth this big deserves company."},
{q:"What had the man seen in his house?", options:["An angel standing and speaking to him","A pillar of fire","Peter appearing in a dream","A dove descending"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:13",verse:"And he shewed us how he had seen an angel in his house, which stood and said unto him, Send men to Joppa, and call for Simon, whose surname is Peter;", insight:"God was arranging both ends of the meeting; the angel prepared Cornelius while the vision prepared Peter."},
{q:"What would Peter's words accomplish for the man's household?", options:["Words, whereby thou and all thy house shall be saved","Riches and lasting honor","Healing from every sickness","Freedom from Roman rule"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:14",verse:"Who shall tell thee words, whereby thou and all thy house shall be saved.", insight:"Salvation came by words, not by wonders; the gospel preached is the gospel that saves."},
{q:"What happened as Peter began to speak?", options:["The Holy Ghost fell on them, as on us at the beginning","The crowd grew angry","Peter lost his voice","The soldiers arrived"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:15",verse:"And as I began to speak, the Holy Ghost fell on them, as on us at the beginning.", insight:"The Spirit fell mid-sermon; God confirmed the message before Peter could finish it."},
{q:"What word of the Lord did Peter then remember?", options:["Ye shall be baptized with the Holy Ghost","Repent, for the kingdom is at hand","Go ye into all the world","Peace be unto you"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:16",verse:"Then remembered I the word of the Lord, how that he said, John indeed baptized with water; but ye shall be baptized with the Holy Ghost.", insight:"Jesus' own promise explained the moment; Scripture interprets experience, not the other way round."},
{q:"What was Peter's closing question to his critics?", options:["What was I, that I could withstand God?","Who are you to judge me?","Have you received the Spirit yourselves?","Will you come with me to Caesarea?"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:17",verse:"Forasmuch then as God gave them the like gift as he did unto us, who believed on the Lord Jesus Christ; what was I, that I could withstand God?", insight:"Peter's defense was simple: this was God's doing, and who was he to block it?"},
{q:"What did the hearers conclude?", options:["Then hath God also to the Gentiles granted repentance unto life","Peter has gone too far this time","The Gentiles must be circumcised","We must investigate this further"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:18",verse:"When they heard these things, they held their peace, and glorified God, saying, Then hath God also to the Gentiles granted repentance unto life.", insight:"Their prejudice melted into praise; when God moves, even critics become worshippers."},
{q:"Where did the believers scattered by Stephen's persecution travel?", options:["Phenice, and Cyprus, and Antioch","Egypt and Arabia","Rome and Athens","Galilee and Samaria only"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:19",verse:"Now they which were scattered abroad upon the persecution that arose about Stephen travelled as far as Phenice, and Cyprus, and Antioch, preaching the word to none but unto the Jews only.", insight:"Persecution scattered them, and they scattered the gospel; suffering became sowing."},
{q:"Whom did the church in Jerusalem send to Antioch?", options:["Barnabas","Peter","James","Stephen"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:22",verse:"Then tidings of these things came unto the ears of the church which was in Jerusalem: and they sent forth Barnabas, that he should go as far as Antioch.", insight:"Jerusalem sent Barnabas, the encourager, to a work that needed encouragement."},
{q:"Where were the disciples first called Christians?", options:["Antioch","Jerusalem","Caesarea","Tarsus"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:26",verse:"And when he had found him, he brought him unto Antioch. And it came to pass, that a whole year they assembled themselves with the church, and taught much people. And the disciples were called Christians first in Antioch.", insight:"The world named them for Christ before they named themselves; let your life earn the label."},
{q:"What did Agabus signify by the Spirit?", options:["Great dearth throughout all the world","The fall of Jerusalem","A persecution under Herod","A coming journey to Rome"], a:0, ref:"Acts 11:28",verse:"And there stood up one of them named Agabus, and signified by the spirit that there should be great dearth throughout all the world: which came to pass in the days of Claudius Caesar.", insight:"Prophecy was given so the church could prepare to give; foreknowledge should feed generosity."}
]},
{n:12, name:"Peter Escapes Prison", seal:{ref:"Acts 12:24",verse:"But the word of God grew and multiplied."}, facts:["Did you know the church prayed 'without ceasing' for Peter, yet when Rhoda announced he was at the gate, they told her she was mad? God answered a prayer they barely believed He would (Acts 12:5, 15).","Did you know Herod Agrippa I, who killed James and seized Peter, died a gruesome death in Caesarea just as Luke records, an event the Jewish historian Josephus also describes (Acts 12:23)?","Did you know John Mark, whose mother Mary's house hosted the prayer meeting, went on to travel with Barnabas and Saul, and early church tradition names him the author of the Gospel of Mark (Acts 12:12, 25)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Herod the king do to the church?", options:["He stretched forth his hands to vex certain of the church","He joined the church at Antioch","He sent gifts to the apostles","He freed all the prisoners"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:1",verse:"Now about that time Herod the king stretched forth his hands to vex certain of the church.", insight:"Persecution starts small, vexing certain ones; Herod tested the waters with the church's blood."},
{q:"Whom did Herod kill with the sword?", options:["James the brother of John","Peter the fisherman","Stephen the deacon","James the Lord's brother"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:2",verse:"And he killed James the brother of John with the sword.", insight:"James, one of the inner three, fell first; faithfulness does not guarantee a long life, only a true one."},
{q:"Why did Herod go on to seize Peter also?", options:["Because he saw it pleased the Jews","Because Peter owed him money","Because the Romans ordered it","Because Peter had fled the city"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:3",verse:"And because he saw it pleased the Jews, he proceeded further to take Peter also. (Then were the days of unleavened bread.)", insight:"Applause became his policy; leaders who govern by cheers will kill to keep them."},
{q:"How many soldiers were set to guard Peter?", options:["Four quaternions, sixteen in all","Two soldiers","A single guard at the door","The whole city garrison"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:4",verse:"And when he had apprehended him, he put him in prison, and delivered him to four quaternions of soldiers to keep him; intending after Easter to bring him forth to the people.", insight:"Sixteen soldiers for one fisherman; heaven laughs at the arithmetic of fear."},
{q:"What was the church doing while Peter sat in prison?", options:["Prayer was made without ceasing of the church unto God for him","They hid in the hills outside the city","They prepared for his funeral","They fled Jerusalem in the night"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:5",verse:"Peter therefore was kept in prison: but prayer was made without ceasing of the church unto God for him.", insight:"The church's real weapon was not a sword but unceasing prayer; pray like the outcome depends on God, because it does."},
{q:"How was Peter sleeping the night before Herod would bring him forth?", options:["Between two soldiers, bound with two chains","Alone in a dark inner cell","With his head upon a stone","On the roof of the prison"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:6",verse:"And when Herod would have brought him forth, the same night Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains: and the keepers before the door kept the prison.", insight:"He slept between guards and under sentence; peace like that only comes from a clear conscience and a praying church."},
{q:"How did the angel wake Peter?", options:["He smote Peter on the side, and raised him up","He called his name softly","He shook the prison walls","He sang a psalm over him"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:7",verse:"And, behold, the angel of the Lord came upon him, and a light shined in the prison: and he smote Peter on the side, and raised him up, saying, Arise up quickly. And his chains fell off from his hands.", insight:"The angel had to nudge him awake; God's rescue sometimes finds us sleeping through the danger."},
{q:"What did the angel command Peter to do?", options:["Gird thyself, and bind on thy sandals, cast thy garment about thee, and follow me","Run for the gate at once","Shout for the guards to come","Stay where thou art and be silent"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:8",verse:"And the angel said unto him, Gird thyself, and bind on thy sandals. And so he did. And he saith unto him, Cast thy garment about thee, and follow me.", insight:"Get dressed and follow; deliverance asks our feet to move, not just our hearts to believe."},
{q:"What did Peter think was happening as he followed?", options:["He thought he saw a vision","He thought he was dreaming","He thought the guards were playing a trick","He thought it was a trap"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:9",verse:"And he went out, and followed him; and wist not that it was true which was done by the angel; but thought he saw a vision.", insight:"The miracle felt too good to be true; sometimes faith must catch up with God's facts."},
{q:"Which gate opened to them of its own accord?", options:["The iron gate that leadeth unto the city","The gate of the temple","The gate of the prison yard","The gate of Herod's palace"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:10",verse:"When they were past the first and the second ward, they came unto the iron gate that leadeth unto the city; which opened to them of his own accord: and they went out, and passed on through one street; and forthwith the angel departed from him.", insight:"Iron gates open on their own when God is the locksmith; no barrier survives His errand."},
{q:"What did Peter know of a surety once the angel departed?", options:["That the Lord hath sent his angel, and hath delivered me out of the hand of Herod","That he had dreamed the whole thing","That the guards had been bribed","That the church had paid his ransom"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:11",verse:"And when Peter was come to himself, he said, Now I know of a surety, that the Lord hath sent his angel, and hath delivered me out of the hand of Herod, and from all the expectation of the people of the Jews.", insight:"Surety came after obedience; Peter understood the miracle only once he had walked through it."},
{q:"To whose house did Peter go?", options:["The house of Mary the mother of John, whose surname was Mark","The house of Cornelius the centurion","The upper room in the temple","The house of Simon the tanner"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:12",verse:"And when he had considered the thing, he came to the house of Mary the mother of John, whose surname was Mark; where many were gathered together praying.", insight:"He went where the praying was; answers head straight for the prayer meeting."},
{q:"Who came to the gate when Peter knocked?", options:["A damsel named Rhoda","Mary the mother of John","A Roman soldier on watch","Peter's own wife"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:13",verse:"And as Peter knocked at the door of the gate, a damsel came to hearken, named Rhoda.", insight:"A servant girl got the first glimpse of the answer; God lets the lowly see it first."},
{q:"Why did Rhoda leave Peter standing at the gate?", options:["She opened not the gate for gladness, but ran in to tell the others","She did not believe it was really him","She was afraid of the soldiers nearby","She had fallen asleep at her post"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:14",verse:"And when she knew Peter’s voice, she opened not the gate for gladness, but ran in, and told how Peter stood before the gate.", insight:"Joy made her forget the gate; sometimes gladness is the most honest theology."},
{q:"What did the praying believers say to Rhoda?", options:["Thou art mad; then, It is his angel","Open the gate this instant","Go back to sleep, child","We knew it all along"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:15",verse:"And they said unto her, Thou art mad. But she constantly affirmed that it was even so. Then said they, It is his angel.", insight:"They prayed for Peter and disbelieved the answer; God answers prayers we barely expect Him to hear."},
{q:"What message did Peter send to James and the brethren?", options:["Go shew these things unto James, and to the brethren","Tell no one what happened tonight","Gather the church together at dawn","Flee Jerusalem before morning"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:17",verse:"But he, beckoning unto them with the hand to hold their peace, declared unto them how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. And he said, Go shew these things unto James, and to the brethren. And he departed, and went into another place.", insight:"Testimony is meant to be shared; what God did for you belongs to the whole family."},
{q:"What did Herod command concerning the keepers?", options:["That they should be put to death","That they be given a reward","That they be sent to Rome","That they be forgiven"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:19",verse:"And when Herod had sought for him, and found him not, he examined the keepers, and commanded that they should be put to death. And he went down from Judaea to Caesarea, and there abode.", insight:"Herod's justice punished the innocent guards; tyrants always bill someone else for their failures."},
{q:"What did the people shout as Herod, arrayed in royal apparel, made his oration?", options:["It is the voice of a god, and not of a man","Long live the king forever","Hosanna to the king","Give us Barabbas"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:22",verse:"And the people gave a shout, saying, It is the voice of a god, and not of a man.", insight:"Flattery crowned him a god; the crowd's praise became his death sentence."},
{q:"Why did the angel of the Lord smite Herod?", options:["Because he gave not God the glory","Because he had killed James","Because he vexed the church","Because he taxed the people"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:23",verse:"And immediately the angel of the Lord smote him, because he gave not God the glory: and he was eaten of worms, and gave up the ghost.", insight:"He stole God's glory and heaven collected; pride that accepts worship invites judgment."},
{q:"What was Herod's end?", options:["He was eaten of worms, and gave up the ghost","He repented and believed","He fled to Rome in disgrace","He died in battle"], a:0, ref:"Acts 12:23",verse:"And immediately the angel of the Lord smote him, because he gave not God the glory: and he was eaten of worms, and gave up the ghost.", insight:"Worms for the man who played god; God writes the last line on every proud story."}
]},
{n:13, name:"The First Missionary Journey", seal:{ref:"Acts 13:47",verse:"For so hath the Lord commanded us, saying, I have set thee to be a light of the Gentiles, that thou shouldest be for salvation unto the ends of the earth."}, facts:["Did you know Saul is first called Paul in Acts 13:9, at the very moment he confronts Elymas, as if the new name marks his new mission to the Gentiles?","Did you know Sergius Paulus was a real Roman proconsul of Cyprus, and an inscription from the island names a Sergius Paulus in office there, matching Luke's careful history (Acts 13:7)?","Did you know Paul's sermon at Pisidian Antioch is the longest recorded sermon in Acts, walking through Israel's whole story from Egypt to David to the empty tomb (Acts 13:16-41)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who were the prophets and teachers in the church at Antioch?", options:["Barnabas, Simeon called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen, and Saul","Peter, James, and John","The seven chosen deacons","Paul and Silas"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:1",verse:"Now there were in the church that was at Antioch certain prophets and teachers; as Barnabas, and Simeon that was called Niger, and Lucius of Cyrene, and Manaen, which had been brought up with Herod the tetrarch, and Saul.", insight:"A multiethnic leadership team; the mission to the nations began with a church that already looked like the nations."},
{q:"What did the Holy Ghost say as they ministered to the Lord and fasted?", options:["Separate me Barnabas and Saul for the work whereunto I have called them","Build a temple here in Antioch","Send Peter at once to Rome","Wait here for a further sign"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:2",verse:"As they ministered to the Lord, and fasted, the Holy Ghost said, Separate me Barnabas and Saul for the work whereunto I have called them.", insight:"The Spirit speaks to a fasting, worshiping church; mission is born in devotion, not in planning meetings."},
{q:"What did the church do before sending them away?", options:["They fasted and prayed, and laid their hands on them","They collected money for the journey","They wrote letters of introduction","They chose men to replace them"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:3",verse:"And when they had fasted and prayed, and laid their hands on them, they sent them away.", insight:"Laying on of hands marked ownership; the whole church sent them, not just their own zeal."},
{q:"Where did Barnabas and Saul sail first?", options:["Unto Seleucia, and from thence to Cyprus","Straight to Rome","To Athens in Greece","To Ephesus in Asia"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:4",verse:"So they, being sent forth by the Holy Ghost, departed unto Seleucia; and from thence they sailed to Cyprus.", insight:"They started with Barnabas's home island; God often launches a calling from familiar ground."},
{q:"Whom did they find when they had gone through the isle unto Paphos?", options:["Bar-jesus, a sorcerer and false prophet","A Roman centurion named Cornelius","A merchant of purple","A Greek philosopher"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:6",verse:"And when they had gone through the isle unto Paphos, they found a certain sorcerer, a false prophet, a Jew, whose name was Bar-jesus:", insight:"The gospel's first stop in Cyprus faced a sorcerer; light always meets its counterfeit first."},
{q:"Who was the deputy of the country?", options:["Sergius Paulus, a prudent man","Felix the governor","Gallio the proconsul","Herod the tetrarch"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:7",verse:"Which was with the deputy of the country, Sergius Paulus, a prudent man; who called for Barnabas and Saul, and desired to hear the word of God.", insight:"A prudent Roman wanted to hear the word; God plants seekers in high places."},
{q:"What was Elymas the sorcerer seeking to do?", options:["To turn away the deputy from the faith","To steal their travel money","To have them arrested","To learn their magic"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:8",verse:"But Elymas the sorcerer (for so is his name by interpretation) withstood them, seeking to turn away the deputy from the faith.", insight:"Opposition to the gospel is rarely neutral; Elymas fought to keep a seeking soul in the dark."},
{q:"Who is also called Paul?", options:["Saul","Barnabas","Silas","John Mark"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:9",verse:"Then Saul, (who also is called Paul,) filled with the Holy Ghost, set his eyes on him,", insight:"From here on Luke calls him Paul; the apostle to the Gentiles steps into his Roman name."},
{q:"What did Paul call Elymas?", options:["Child of the devil, thou enemy of all righteousness","A blind guide of the blind","A son of Belial","A wolf in sheep's clothing"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:10",verse:"And said, O full of all subtilty and all mischief, thou child of the devil, thou enemy of all righteousness, wilt thou not cease to pervert the right ways of the Lord?", insight:"Paul named the evil plainly; love for the seeker sometimes requires war on the deceiver."},
{q:"What judgment fell upon Elymas?", options:["He was made blind, not seeing the sun for a season","He was struck dumb on the spot","He fell down dead","He was cast into prison"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:11",verse:"And now, behold, the hand of the Lord is upon thee, and thou shalt be blind, not seeing the sun for a season. And immediately there fell on him a mist and a darkness; and he went about seeking some to lead him by the hand.", insight:"The man who spread darkness was given darkness; God's judgments fit the crime."},
{q:"What did the deputy do when he saw what was done?", options:["He believed, being astonished at the doctrine of the Lord","He had Paul arrested at once","He fled the island in fear","He demanded a still greater sign"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:12",verse:"Then the deputy, when he saw what was done, believed, being astonished at the doctrine of the Lord.", insight:"It was the doctrine, not just the miracle, that won him; truth astonishes longer than wonders."},
{q:"Where did John depart from Paul and his company?", options:["At Perga in Pamphylia, returning to Jerusalem","At Antioch in Pisidia","On the island of Cyprus","At the city of Iconium"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:13",verse:"Now when Paul and his company loosed from Paphos, they came to Perga in Pamphylia: and John departing from them returned to Jerusalem.", insight:"John Mark's leaving would later split the team; even painful exits are in God's story."},
{q:"About how long did God suffer Israel's manners in the wilderness?", options:["About forty years","About four hundred years","About seventy years","About twelve years"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:18",verse:"And about the time of forty years suffered he their manners in the wilderness.", insight:"Forty years of patience with a grumbling people; God's longsuffering is the backdrop of the whole sermon."},
{q:"How many nations did God destroy in the land of Canaan?", options:["Seven","Twelve","Three","Forty"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:19",verse:"And when he had destroyed seven nations in the land of Chanaan, he divided their land to them by lot.", insight:"Seven nations fell so one promise could stand; God's faithfulness has a long memory."},
{q:"About how long did the judges rule over Israel?", options:["About four hundred and fifty years","About forty years","About seventy years","About a thousand years"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:20",verse:"And after that he gave unto them judges about the space of four hundred and fifty years, until Samuel the prophet.", insight:"Four and a half centuries of judges; God kept raising deliverers for a forgetful people."},
{q:"How does God describe David?", options:["A man after mine own heart, which shall fulfil all my will","The greatest warrior of Israel","A prophet like unto Moses","The wisest of all kings"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:22",verse:"And when he had removed him, he raised up unto them David to be their king; to whom also he gave testimony, and said, I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after mine own heart, which shall fulfil all my will.", insight:"God's commendation of David was about the heart, not the record; obedience matters more than achievements."},
{q:"What did God do to Jesus after men had laid him in a sepulchre?", options:["God raised him from the dead","God hid his body from men","God sent angels to guard the tomb","God avenged him at once"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:30",verse:"But God raised him from the dead:", insight:"The sermon turns on this hinge: men buried Him, but God raised Him."},
{q:"What is preached unto you through this man?", options:["The forgiveness of sins","The keeping of the law","The rebuilding of the temple","The overthrow of Rome"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:38",verse:"Be it known unto you therefore, men and brethren, that through this man is preached unto you the forgiveness of sins:", insight:"Forgiveness, not reform, is the offer; the gospel gives what the law could only demand."},
{q:"How many came together the next sabbath day to hear the word of God?", options:["Almost the whole city","Only the Jews of the synagogue","A handful of proselytes","The city rulers alone"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:44",verse:"And the next sabbath day came almost the whole city together to hear the word of God.", insight:"Almost a whole city turned out; hunger for the word can empty the streets into the synagogue."},
{q:"What did Paul and Barnabas say when the Jews contradicted and blasphemed?", options:["Lo, we turn to the Gentiles","We will preach here no more","We return to Jerusalem","We appeal unto Caesar"], a:0, ref:"Acts 13:46",verse:"Then Paul and Barnabas waxed bold, and said, It was necessary that the word of God should first have been spoken to you: but seeing ye put it from you, and judge yourselves unworthy of everlasting life, lo, we turn to the Gentiles.", insight:"Rejection by some became an open door to others; God's plan moves forward through closed doors."}
]},
{n:14, name:"Through Much Tribulation", seal:{ref:"Acts 14:22",verse:"Confirming the souls of the disciples, and exhorting them to continue in the faith, and that we must through much tribulation enter into the kingdom of God."}, facts:["Did you know Lystra had no synagogue, so Paul preached to pagans straight from creation instead of Scripture, the first recorded sermon to a purely Gentile crowd (Acts 14:15-17)?","Did you know Paul was stoned at Lystra, dragged out of the city as dead, and walked back into the city the same day? Timothy, who later joined Paul, came from this very town and likely saw it all (Acts 14:19-20; 16:1).","Did you know this chapter gives the pattern for finishing a mission: revisit the converts, warn them of tribulation, and ordain elders in every church before sailing home (Acts 14:21-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did Paul and Barnabas go first in Iconium?", options:["Into the synagogue of the Jews","To the public marketplace","To the governor's palace","To the temple of Jupiter"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:1",verse:"And it came to pass in Iconium, that they went both together into the synagogue of the Jews, and so spake, that a great multitude both of the Jews and also of the Greeks believed.", insight:"They started where the Scriptures were known; the synagogue was the mission's front door."},
{q:"What did the unbelieving Jews do?", options:["They stirred up the Gentiles, and made their minds evil affected against the brethren","They believed and were baptized","They left the city in peace","They wrote to the emperor"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:2",verse:"But the unbelieving Jews stirred up the Gentiles, and made their minds evil affected against the brethren.", insight:"Unbelief rarely stays quiet; it recruits. Guard your mind against secondhand bitterness."},
{q:"How long did they therefore abide in Iconium?", options:["Long time, speaking boldly in the Lord","Only one sabbath day","Forty days and nights","Until the winter came"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:3",verse:"Long time therefore abode they speaking boldly in the Lord, which gave testimony unto the word of his grace, and granted signs and wonders to be done by their hands.", insight:"Boldness plus patience; they did not flee at the first sign of trouble."},
{q:"What did their enemies plan to do to them?", options:["To use them despitefully, and to stone them","To fine them heavily","To banish them from the synagogue","To report them to Rome"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:5",verse:"And when there was an assault made both of the Gentiles, and also of the Jews with their rulers, to use them despitefully, and to stone them,", insight:"The same city that heard gladly plotted cruelly; popularity is a thin shield."},
{q:"Where did they flee when they were aware of the assault?", options:["Unto Lystra and Derbe, cities of Lycaonia","Back to Antioch in Syria","Up to Jerusalem","To the island of Cyprus"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:6",verse:"They were ware of it, and fled unto Lystra and Derbe, cities of Lycaonia, and unto the region that lieth round about:", insight:"Fleeing was wisdom, not cowardice; there were other cities, and the gospel had to travel."},
{q:"Who sat at Lystra listening to Paul speak?", options:["A man impotent in his feet, being a cripple from his mother's womb, who never had walked","A Roman soldier on duty","The priest of Jupiter","A wealthy merchant"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:8",verse:"And there sat a certain man at Lystra, impotent in his feet, being a cripple from his mother’s womb, who never had walked:", insight:"A lifetime cripple became the stage for grace; God loves hopeless cases."},
{q:"What did Paul perceive as he steadfastly beheld the man?", options:["That he had faith to be healed","That he was only pretending","That he had fallen asleep","That he was angry at the preaching"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:9",verse:"The same heard Paul speak: who stedfastly beholding him, and perceiving that he had faith to be healed,", insight:"Paul saw faith before he saw the miracle; sometimes the heart rises before the feet do."},
{q:"What did Paul say with a loud voice?", options:["Stand upright on thy feet","Be thou healed this instant","Rise up and walk","In the name of Jesus, arise"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:10",verse:"Said with a loud voice, Stand upright on thy feet. And he leaped and walked.", insight:"A plain command, and legs that never walked obeyed; the word of faith carries God's power."},
{q:"What did the people of Lystra lift up their voices to say?", options:["The gods are come down to us in the likeness of men","Crucify him, crucify him","A prophet is risen among us","Blessed be the God of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:11",verse:"And when the people saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voices, saying in the speech of Lycaonia, The gods are come down to us in the likeness of men.", insight:"They read the miracle through their myths; a true wonder still needs a true explanation."},
{q:"Whom did they call Jupiter, and whom Mercurius?", options:["Barnabas they called Jupiter, and Paul Mercurius, because he was the chief speaker","Paul they called Jupiter, and Barnabas Mercurius","Both of them they called Apollo","Silas they called Jupiter, and Timothy Mercurius"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:12",verse:"And they called Barnabas, Jupiter; and Paul, Mercurius, because he was the chief speaker.", insight:"The talker got the messenger god's name; even pagans honored the preacher's gift."},
{q:"What did the priest of Jupiter bring unto the gates?", options:["Oxen and garlands, to do sacrifice with the people","Gold and silver vessels","Bread and wine for a feast","Branches of palm"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:13",verse:"Then the priest of Jupiter, which was before their city, brought oxen and garlands unto the gates, and would have done sacrifice with the people.", insight:"Worship was one breath away; flattery can turn to idolatry before you notice."},
{q:"How did Barnabas and Paul react to the sacrifice?", options:["They rent their clothes, and ran in among the people, crying out","They accepted the honor quietly","They fled the city at once","They sat down to eat with the priest"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:14",verse:"Which when the apostles, Barnabas and Paul, heard of, they rent their clothes, and ran in among the people, crying out,", insight:"They tore their clothes, not their ticket stubs; true servants refuse worship, even friendly worship."},
{q:"What did they preach to the crowd?", options:["Turn from these vanities unto the living God, which made heaven, and earth, and the sea, and all things that are therein","Offer your sacrifices to Jupiter instead","Submit yourselves to the law of Moses","Return quietly to your homes"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:15",verse:"And saying, Sirs, why do ye these things? We also are men of like passions with you, and preach unto you that ye should turn from these vanities unto the living God, which made heaven, and earth, and the sea, and all things that are therein:", insight:"From vanities to the living God; the gospel names both what to leave and whom to find."},
{q:"How had God not left himself without witness to the nations?", options:["He did good, and gave us rain from heaven, and fruitful seasons, filling our hearts with food and gladness","He had sent them the Scriptures","He had given them the law","He had raised up prophets among them"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:17",verse:"Nevertheless he left not himself without witness, in that he did good, and gave us rain from heaven, and fruitful seasons, filling our hearts with food and gladness.", insight:"Rain and harvests are sermons too; creation preaches to those who never heard a prophet."},
{q:"What did the Jews from Antioch and Iconium do to Paul?", options:["They stoned him, and drew him out of the city, supposing he had been dead","They had him arrested by the rulers","They debated him publicly","They bribed the crowd against him"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:19",verse:"And there came thither certain Jews from Antioch and Iconium, who persuaded the people, and, having stoned Paul, drew him out of the city, supposing he had been dead.", insight:"One day sacrifices, the next day stones; crowds are weather, not climate."},
{q:"What did Paul do after being stoned?", options:["He rose up, and came into the city: and the next day he departed with Barnabas to Derbe","He was buried by the disciples","He sailed home to Tarsus","He lay in bed for a full month"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:20",verse:"Howbeit, as the disciples stood round about him, he rose up, and came into the city: and the next day he departed with Barnabas to Derbe.", insight:"Stoned one day, preaching the next; grace does not keep office hours."},
{q:"Which cities did they return to after preaching at Derbe?", options:["Lystra, and Iconium, and Antioch","Jerusalem and Samaria","Ephesus and Corinth","Rome and Athens"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:21",verse:"And when they had preached the gospel to that city, and had taught many, they returned again to Lystra, and to Iconium, and Antioch,", insight:"They went back through the danger zone; new churches need strengthening, not just starting."},
{q:"What did they exhort the disciples to continue in?", options:["The faith, and that we must through much tribulation enter into the kingdom of God","The hope that suffering would soon end","The belief that Rome would convert","The promise of coming wealth"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:22",verse:"Confirming the souls of the disciples, and exhorting them to continue in the faith, and that we must through much tribulation enter into the kingdom of God.", insight:"Tribulation is the doorway, not the detour; the kingdom is entered, not eased into."},
{q:"What did they ordain in every church?", options:["Elders, with prayer and fasting","Deacons only, and no elders","A single bishop for each city","No leaders at all"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:23",verse:"And when they had ordained them elders in every church, and had prayed with fasting, they commended them to the Lord, on whom they believed.", insight:"Every church got elders, chosen with fasting; leadership is prayed over, not rushed."},
{q:"What did they rehearse to the church at Antioch?", options:["All that God had done with them, and how he had opened the door of faith unto the Gentiles","How much money they had collected","How the Romans had protected them","How they had escaped from Herod"], a:0, ref:"Acts 14:27",verse:"And when they were come, and had gathered the church together, they rehearsed all that God had done with them, and how he had opened the door of faith unto the Gentiles.", insight:"God opened the door; they just walked through it. All mission reports should sound like that."}
]},
{n:15, name:"The Jerusalem Council", seal:{ref:"Acts 15:11",verse:"But we believe that through the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ we shall be saved, even as they."}, facts:["Did you know the Jerusalem Council was the church's first great doctrinal debate, and its answer still stands: Gentiles are saved by grace through faith, with no circumcision required (Acts 15:11)?","Did you know the council asked Gentile believers to abstain from only four things, idol food, blood, strangled meat, and sexual immorality, so Jewish and Gentile believers could share a table in peace (Acts 15:20, 29)?","Did you know the quarrel over John Mark did not end the story? Barnabas took Mark to Cyprus, Paul chose Silas, and years later Paul would call Mark 'profitable to me for the ministry' (Acts 15:39-40; 2 Timothy 4:11)."], questions:[
{q:"What did certain men which came down from Judaea teach the brethren?", options:["Except ye be circumcised after the manner of Moses, ye cannot be saved","The Gentiles must keep the sabbath day","The temple must be rebuilt at once","Paul is a false apostle"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:1",verse:"And certain men which came down from Judaea taught the brethren, and said, Except ye be circumcised after the manner of Moses, ye cannot be saved.", insight:"They added one requirement to grace and broke the gospel; 'Jesus plus' is 'Jesus minus.'"},
{q:"Who went up to Jerusalem unto the apostles and elders about this question?", options:["Paul and Barnabas, and certain other of them","Peter and John alone","The whole church of Antioch","Silas and Timothy"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:2",verse:"When therefore Paul and Barnabas had no small dissension and disputation with them, they determined that Paul and Barnabas, and certain other of them, should go up to Jerusalem unto the apostles and elders about this question.", insight:"They carried the dispute to the apostles; big questions deserve the church's best minds, not its loudest voices."},
{q:"Who rose up saying the Gentiles must be circumcised and keep the law of Moses?", options:["Certain of the sect of the Pharisees which believed","The Sadducees of Jerusalem","The Roman authorities","The priests of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:5",verse:"But there rose up certain of the sect of the Pharisees which believed, saying, That it was needful to circumcise them, and to command them to keep the law of Moses.", insight:"Believers can still be wrong; old habits of law-keeping die hard even in saved hearts."},
{q:"What did Peter say God had chosen him to do?", options:["That the Gentiles by his mouth should hear the word of the gospel, and believe","To preach the gospel only to the Jews","To write the council's letter","To circumcise the new converts"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:7",verse:"And when there had been much disputing, Peter rose up, and said unto them, Men and brethren, ye know how that a good while ago God made choice among us, that the Gentiles by my mouth should hear the word of the gospel, and believe.", insight:"Peter's own story was the evidence; God had already voted with the Spirit at Cornelius's house."},
{q:"What witness did God, which knoweth the hearts, give the Gentiles?", options:["He gave them the Holy Ghost, even as he did unto us","He gave them the temple at Jerusalem","He gave them circumcision","He gave them the promised land"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:8",verse:"And God, which knoweth the hearts, bare them witness, giving them the Holy Ghost, even as he did unto us;", insight:"The same Spirit, the same gift; God does not run a two-tier kingdom."},
{q:"How did God purify their hearts?", options:["By faith","By circumcision","By keeping the law","By washing in the temple"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:9",verse:"And put no difference between us and them, purifying their hearts by faith.", insight:"Faith purifies; no ritual washes the inside of a person."},
{q:"What did Peter call the yoke they wanted to put on the disciples?", options:["A yoke which neither our fathers nor we were able to bear","A light and easy burden","A schoolmaster for all time","A holy and sweet delight"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:10",verse:"Now therefore why tempt ye God, to put a yoke upon the neck of the disciples, which neither our fathers nor we were able to bear?", insight:"Peter called it unbearable because he had tried to bear it; honesty about the law leads to grace."},
{q:"How shall we be saved?", options:["Through the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ","Through circumcision joined with grace","Through keeping the law of Moses","Through the prayers of the apostles"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:11",verse:"But we believe that through the grace of the Lord Jesus Christ we shall be saved, even as they.", insight:"Grace alone, for us and for them; one door, one key, for every nation."},
{q:"Who answered after Barnabas and Paul had held their peace?", options:["James","Peter","John","Andrew"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:13",verse:"And after they had held their peace, James answered, saying, Men and brethren, hearken unto me:", insight:"James, the Lord's brother, summed up the council; wisdom often speaks last and settles most."},
{q:"What had Simeon declared?", options:["How God at the first did visit the Gentiles, to take out of them a people for his name","That the temple would surely fall","That Paul should go to Rome","That the law would endure forever"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:14",verse:"Simeon hath declared how God at the first did visit the Gentiles, to take out of them a people for his name.", insight:"A people for His name, taken from the nations; the church was always in God's plan."},
{q:"What will God build again?", options:["The tabernacle of David, which is fallen down","The temple of Solomon in gold","The walls of Jerusalem","The kingdom of Israel at once"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:16",verse:"After this I will return, and will build again the tabernacle of David, which is fallen down; and I will build again the ruins thereof, and I will set it up:", insight:"The fallen tent of David rises again in Christ; prophecy finds its yes in Jesus."},
{q:"What was James's sentence?", options:["That we trouble not them, which from among the Gentiles are turned to God","That they all be circumcised","That they keep the whole law","That they leave the church"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:19",verse:"Wherefore my sentence is, that we trouble not them, which from among the Gentiles are turned to God:", insight:"'Trouble not them'; the council's great word was freedom, not a longer rulebook."},
{q:"From what were the Gentile believers to abstain?", options:["Pollutions of idols, and from fornication, and from things strangled, and from blood","Pork, wine, work on the sabbath, and idols","Taxes, oaths, war, and trade","Temple visits, feasts, fasts, and tithes"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:20",verse:"But that we write unto them, that they abstain from pollutions of idols, and from fornication, and from things strangled, and from blood.", insight:"Four abstentions for the sake of fellowship; love limits its liberty at the shared table."},
{q:"Who was sent to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas?", options:["Judas surnamed Barsabas, and Silas, chief men among the brethren","Peter and John the apostles","Timothy and Titus","Luke and Aristarchus"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:22",verse:"Then pleased it the apostles and elders, with the whole church, to send chosen men of their own company to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas; namely, Judas surnamed Barsabas, and Silas, chief men among the brethren:", insight:"They sent living letters with the written one; truth travels best with trusted faces."},
{q:"How are Barnabas and Paul described in the council's letter?", options:["Men that have hazarded their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ","Learned men of the law","Wealthy supporters of the church","Roman citizens of high rank"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:26",verse:"Men that have hazarded their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ.", insight:"They had gambled their lives on Jesus' name; the council honored courage it had not shown."},
{q:"What seemed good to the Holy Ghost, and to the council?", options:["To lay upon you no greater burden than these necessary things","To require full circumcision","To send missionaries to every nation","To meet every year in Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:28",verse:"For it seemed good to the Holy Ghost, and to us, to lay upon you no greater burden than these necessary things;", insight:"The Spirit's yoke is light; when leaders add weight, check whether heaven signed it."},
{q:"How did the multitude at Antioch receive the epistle?", options:["They rejoiced for the consolation","They argued about its meaning","They burned it in the fire","They sent it back unopened"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:31",verse:"Which when they had read, they rejoiced for the consolation.", insight:"Consolation, not controversy; good doctrine lands like relief."},
{q:"Whom did Barnabas determine to take with them on the next journey?", options:["John, whose surname was Mark","Silas the prophet","Timothy the young disciple","Luke the physician"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:37",verse:"And Barnabas determined to take with them John, whose surname was Mark.", insight:"Barnabas, the encourager, would not give up on Mark; grace gives second chances names."},
{q:"Why did Paul think it not good to take Mark with them?", options:["He departed from them from Pamphylia, and went not with them to the work","He was too young for the journey","He was not circumcised","He had fallen sick at Antioch"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:38",verse:"But Paul thought not good to take him with them, who departed from them from Pamphylia, and went not with them to the work.", insight:"Paul valued proven faithfulness; the mission field is no place to test a quitter."},
{q:"What followed the sharp contention between Paul and Barnabas?", options:["They departed asunder one from the other: and Barnabas took Mark, and sailed unto Cyprus","They made peace and traveled on together","Barnabas retired from the work","Paul sailed home to Tarsus alone"], a:0, ref:"Acts 15:39",verse:"And the contention was so sharp between them, that they departed asunder one from the other: and so Barnabas took Mark, and sailed unto Cyprus;", insight:"Even apostles part ways; God used the split to double the teams."}
]}
]);
